- `constructor-unit-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests`

**How to implement.** Red first for 001 §B 'Physics is pure data' (.spec-md §3.1): a tabulated import becomes axis data. Facts only; no production file changes. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs` (module `MaterialImportTests`, beside the tabulated facts at `:35-59`) add three facts. (1) `a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`: `(readYaml "Si.yml").importMaterial` MUST be `Ok entry` whose `entry.complexity` is `Some c` with `c.eps = EpsWithDispValue (IsotropicDispersive [ segment ])`, `c.magnetic = None` and `c.active = None`; `segment.wavelengthInterval.lower.value` and `.upper.value` MUST be the first and last tabulated wavelengths of `fixtures/Si.yml` (0.250 µm and 0.700 µm) in metres, within 1e-15 m; `c.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864`) MUST be false, because a table is not editable term data, and the import stays view-only as its `complexity = None` keeps it today (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:193`); and `entry.properties.epsWithDisp.getEps w` MUST equal `c.toProperties.epsWithDisp.getEps w` at every tabulated wavelength (the seed invariant `properties = complexity.toProperties`). The fact MUST NOT name an `EpsAxisDispersion` case that does not exist yet, so it compiles on the start tree. (2) `an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`: the same assertions over `(readCsv "sample-nk.csv").importMaterial` and its range, 400 nm to 700 nm. (3) `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours`: for every row of `Si.yml` and of `sample-nk.csv`, `epsAt entry` at the row's wavelength MUST equal `nkSquared` of the row's n and k, and at the midpoint of every pair of neighbouring rows it MUST equal `nkSquared` of the two rows' mean n and mean k, each within the file's `closeC 1e-12`. The fact writes the rows out from the fixtures; it does not parse the fixtures a second way. Facts (1) and (2) are red on the start tree, because `entryFromTabulated` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:183-194`) sets `complexity = None`. Fact (3) passes on the start tree's closure (`buildTabulatedClosure`, `:158-179`) and MUST stay green when the closure becomes data in step 2: it proves that no number moves.

**Acceptance.** After the three facts land, constructor-unit-tests (MaterialImportTests) MUST fail with exactly `a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range` and `an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`, each failing on a `None` complexity; `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours` and every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.
